= HL7 Diff Tool
John Emmanuel <john.x.emmanueljd@questdiagnostics.com>
v1.0, September 2025: Initial release
:showtitlepage:
:notitle:
:noheader:
:nofooter:

== Overview

A tool to compare two HL7 message files and highlight differences based on configurable rules.

=== Rules to be supported

- compare by hl7 profiles (v2.5.1, v2.5, v2.3 etc)
- highlight a particular field in every message
- equalling or containing a certain value, or when it actually has any value
- “not” indicator and highlight where it is not a certain value or doesn’t have a value
-  highlight a date field, I get options that are more suitable to date values, such as greater than or less than
-  red colour highlight is reserved for invalid values,  
- trim spaces
- ignore spaces
- ignore blank lines
- ignore case
- ignore EOL differences
- align similar lines
- ignore missing trailing EOL
- ignore comment differences
- ignore extra records from either file
- ignore segments empty trailing fields
- ignore fields with specific patterns (Patterns have to be separated by comma)
- ignore specific segments and fields
- ignore trailing component separators
- apply filters using all records / different records only

== Design Notes

=== Domain Model

- HL7Message

Represents a parsed HL7 message. Internally stores segments and fields in a structured format (e.g., a dictionary or tree).

[source,java]
----
public class HL7Message {
    private List<HL7Segment> segments;

    public static HL7Message parse(String rawMessage);
    public List<HL7Segment> getSegments();
}
----

- HL7Segment

Represents a single segment (MSH|...,PID|...,etc.) with fields

[source,java]
----
public class HL7Segment {
    private String name;
    private List<String> fields;

    public String getName();
    public List<String> getFields();
}
----


=== Comparison Engine

- HL7Comparator

Entry point for comparing two HL7 messages.

[source,java]
----
public class HL7Comparator {
    private List<ComparisonRule> rules;

    public ComparisonResult compare(HL7Message msg1, HL7Message msg2);
    public void addRule(ComparisonRule rule);
}
----

- ComparisonRule

Interface for defining comparison rules.

[source,java]
----
public interface ComparisonRule {
    void apply(HL7ComparisonContext context);
}
----

- HL7ComparisonContext

Hold state during comparison, including messages and differences found.

[source,java]
----
public class HL7ComparisonContext {
    private HL7Message msg1;
    private HL7Message msg2;
    private List<ComparisonDifference> differences;

    public void addDifference(ComparisonDifference diff);
    public List<ComparisonDifference> getDifferences();
}
----

- ComparisonDifference

Encapsulates a single difference found during comparison.

[source,java]
----
public class ComparisonDifference {
    private String segmentName;
    private int fieldIndex;
    
    private String leftValue;
    private String rightValue;
    
    private TextRange leftRange;
    private TextRange rightRange;
    
    private String description;
}
----

- TextRange

Represents start-end positions for highlighting differences (absolute or relative).

[source,java]
----
public class TextRange {
    private int startOffset;
    private int endOffset;

    public int length() { return endOffset - startOffset;}
}
----

- ComparisonResult

Encapsulates the overall result of a comparison.

[source,java]
----
public class ComparisonResult {
    private boolean equal;
    private List<ComparisonDifference> differences;

    public boolean isEqual();
    public List<ComparisonDifference> getDifferences();
}
----

== Highlighting Engine

The engine consumes ComparisonResult and produces output for visualizations.

[source,java]
----
public interface HighlightEngine {
    public String render(String originalText, List<ComparisonDifference> differences);ComparisonResult result);
}
----

=== Implementations

- NoHighlightEngine - returns plain text.
- ConsoleHighlightEngine - ANSI color codes for CLI.
- HTMLHighlightEngine - Wraps differences in <span class="diff"> for web UIs.
- JsonHighlightEngine - Produces structured JSON with marked ranges.
- JUnitAssertHelper - Generates JUnit assertions for automated tests.

=== Supported types of Highlighting
Defines highlighting strategies.

[source,java]
----
public enum HighlightType {
    INLINE, // replaces in-line (html, ansi console)
    BLOCK, // show blocks of text with diffs marked
    STRUCTURED // JSON / object model highlighting
}
----

== Workflow

1. Parse raw messages into HL7Message objects using HL7Message.parse().

2. Build comparator with desired rules.

[source,java]
----
HL7Comparator comparator = new HL7Comparator(List.of(
    new IgnoreWhitespaceRule(),
    new IgnoreCaseRule(),
    new IgnoreTrailingEmptyFieldsRule(),
    new HighlightFieldRule("PID-5"), // Example: highlight patient name field
    new DateComparisonRule("OBR-7"),   // Example: date field comparison
    new IgnorePatternRule("\\d{14}")
));
----

3. Run comparison.

[source,java]
----
ComparisonResult result = comparator.compare(msg1, msg2);
----

4. Inspect results

- result.isEqual() indicates if messages are equivalent based on rules.
- List of differences can be formatted for display.

== Adding new rules

- Implement ComparisonRule interface.
- Rules are chainable and can modify comparison context.
- Could provide a DSL-like builder for configuring rules easily.

[source,java]
----
HL7Comparator comparator = new HL7Comparator.Builder()
    .ignoreWhitespace()
    .ignoreBlankLines()
    .ignoreTrailingEmptyFields()
    .ignoreCase()
    .highlightField("PID-5")
    .ignorePattern("\\d{14}")
    .allowExtraSegments()
    .build();
----

== Advanced features

- Segment alignment strategies:
    - Strict order
    - Flexible alignment (find best matching PID segments)
- Pluggable difference reporters:
    - Human-readable text
    - JSON report for APIs
    - JUnit assert helper for tests
- Profiles:
    - Predefined rule sets for common HL7 versions (2.3, 2.5, 2.5.1)
    - Predefined rule sets (strict, lenient, tolerant)


